The black group in question consists of the connected stones at B3, B4, C1 and C2 (A2 is isolated and irrelevant to capture). This group has exactly four liberties: A3, A4, B1 and B2.  

White’s only forcing first move that reduces those liberties while creating unavoidable follow-up threats (regardless of Black’s replies) is B2. Any other candidate (A3, A4, B1, etc.) leaves Black at least one safe response that preserves two or more liberties and allows escape or connection. After White B2 the remaining liberties become three and every subsequent Black answer permits White to continue filling them in a sequence that ends with capture; therefore B2 is the unique initiating move.

