The C1-C2 black group starts with exactly two liberties at B1 and B2. White’s placement at B2 fills one shared liberty and puts the stones in atari while leaving the new white stone itself with the still-open B1 as a legal liberty. Black’s only reply that avoids immediate capture is to take the single white stone at B1. White then simply refills at B2; because the capture has removed C1 and C2, that refill is legal and leaves the enlarged black group (now including A2-B3-B4) with no remaining internal eye space and no way to reconnect.  

Any other first move leaves at least one black group an extra liberty or an escape route. In particular, starting at B1 lets Black answer at B2, linking everything into a single chain whose external liberties (A1, A3, A4) are no longer forced to zero. The same holds for A3, A1, or C5: each permits Black a safe reply that either creates an eye or links out. Thus only B2 initiates a forcing sequence that captures against every possible Black defense.

